Solutions to all six questions of the <University of Oxford> Part A <metric space> and <complex analysis> paper, sat on 14 June 2021. Source: https://www.whatdotheyknow.com/request/bsc_mathematics_part_a_examinati/response/2820674/attach/3/FOI%20202410%20944%20Data.pdf#page=54[released examination PDF, compilation pages 54–58; paper pages 1–5]. The examination counted the best four answers; all six are covered here. The printed request in 6(c)(i) is impossible for the stated planar domain: its solution proves this and gives the precise map obtained when the missing point at infinity is accounted for.

